--- !u!114 &443914527868320527
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1106199154083465787}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0882748dc185476197f6ec16b90304dd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  notesText: 'In the Distance Detector, we''re using two different ways to perform
    multiple actions when an event fires.


    We have wired up several actions
    in the Inspector for when the UFO notices the player.


    We have wired up
    only one action in the inspector for when the UFO forgets the player.  However,
    if you read the code, that single action just performs several sub-actions under
    the hood.


    You can use either pattern depending on your needs.  Keeping
    everything in the Inspector might be easier for some designers.  Moving it to
    code might work better with source control.'
